abstract: >-
  Periodic orbits of the planar three-body problem with zero angular
  momentum that are in none of the published lists, each verified to
  30 digits, with linear stability from the monodromy matrix. Among them
  a linearly stable orbit at masses 1 : 1 : 4 (T = 53.2548543044, stability
  indices 0.0501 and -0.0599); it is the continuation in m3 of the orbit
  I.A-5 listed at masses 1 : 1 : 2, stable for m3 from about 3.74 to 4.18.
  Includes the search engine, the
  30-digit verification and test batteries against published
  high-precision data. Code and computations were written with Claude,
  an AI model by Anthropic.
